# This is a Nex page

You are reading this at nex://localhost:11900/: served to you by the Unseen Servant (usv) Nex server.

## Unseen Servant, and why "usv"

Unseen Servant is a small server that publishes one folder of writing to several internet protocols at once. The short name takes the letters from the long one:

```
UnSeen serVant  ->  u  s  v
```

It is abbreviated rather than spelled out because it is also a command you type.

## About Nex

Nex is the smallest thing that still works: send a path, get bytes, the connection closes. No status codes, no content types, no headers. It is explicitly telnet-compatible, so you can speak it by hand, and the whole protocol fits in your head, which is the reason people like it.

=> https://nightfall.city/nex/info/specification.txt The Nex specification

## Reading Nex natively

If this page arrived looking strange, you may be reading it through a gateway. These clients speak Nex directly:

=> https://git.sr.ht/~hedy/gelim gelim (terminal)
=> https://codeberg.org/luxferre/BFG BFG (terminal)

Client support changes; this list was checked in August 2026.

## The same writing, other protocols

This is one folder of writing, rendered to each of these. The hostname never changes, the scheme at the front picks the protocol and the port:

* Gemini: gemini://localhost:11965/
* Gopher: gopher://localhost:17070/
* Spartan: spartan://localhost:13300/
* Finger: finger://localhost:17979
* Web: https://localhost/

